From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:35:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 075/112] Settings > Firmware version: readable on the OLED, on
 up to three lines

The version string was squeezed onto one line with
drawStringCentredShrinkIfNecessary(): "1.2.1-mastertune-v17-l2d-b3385d83"
(33 characters) got 128 / 33 = 3 pixels per character of the 6 the small
font needs, so the letters overlapped into garble (v16 L2: 42 characters).

Now drawLinesBrokenAtDashes() draws it in the normal small menu font
(6 x 7 pixels, 9 from line to line), broken after a '-' (the '-' stays at
the end of the line), at most 21 characters a line and three lines: as few
lines as it takes, then as even as they can be ("1.2.1-mastertune-" /
"v17-l2d-b3385d83"), each line centred, the block centred below the title.
A part longer than a line without a '-' is cut where the line is full; up
to 63 characters fit. The 7-segment display scrolls the string as before.

Tested in the emulator (tests/settings/firmware_version_emu.py): the menu
item's own render and the 33-, 42- and 48-character strings, from the
canvas calls and the OLED image; 41 of 41 checks (v17: 6 fail).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
